{"id":"punk-2021","slug":"punk-2021","sub":null,"name":"Punk Protocol","date":"2021-08-10","one_liner":"A front-running bot copied the Punk Protocol attacker's pool takeover and landed at index 50 vs his 52 in block 12995895 (43.33 vs 40.00 gwei): $5.95M USDT+DAI taken, $4.95M returned, $1M kept; it also mis-sent $3.0M USDC to the attacker. Pre-Merge, in-block evidence only.","bot":"anonymous white-hat front-running bot (EOA 0x3aa27ab2, contract 0x00000000b2ff)","race_type":"beat-pending-attack","narrative":"Real attacker: EOA 0x1d5a5640... (funded from the Tornado Cash 0.1 ETH pool) deployed contract 0x1695ce70... in block 12994067 and called it in tx 0x7604c7dd at block 12995895, index 52 (40.0 gwei max fee). The bot's tx 0x597d11c0 (EOA 0x3aa27ab2..., contract 0x00000000b2ff..., effective price 43.33 gwei, type-2 tx with maxFee 66.70 / maxPriority 13.30) sits at index 50 of the same block. Call-tree diff (incidents/punk-2021/call_diff.json): the bot makes the same 9 victim calls in the same pool order (USDC, USDT, DAI pools: initialize -> invest -> withdrawToForge) with identical initialize() arguments 1-5; only argument 0 (the new 'forge') is its own contract instead of the attacker's. It also left the attacker's own EOA 0x1d5a5640 as the recipient of the USDC transfer (2,995,824.696852 USDC) while sending USDT and DAI to its own EOA: that recipient exists only in the attacker's tx, so the bot's tx was derived from it. The attacker's tx still succeeded but was left with dust (0.0288 USDC, 0.0369 USDT, 0.0304 DAI). Anvil replay on a fork of block 12995894: attacker alone would have received 2,995,824.73 USDC + 3,000,022.82 USDT + 2,954,191.57 DAI; bot-then-attacker reproduces the chain exactly; attacker-then-bot makes the bot's tx revert. The bot's own on-chain messages ('I frontran the real attacker', 'Fixed the bug in my bot which kept your USDC transfer in place') and Punk's incident report confirm it. Ordering is a plain gas-price auction (effective price 43.33 vs 40.00 gwei, no coinbase payment, no bundle-like pattern); there is no pre-Merge mempool archive, so whether the bot saw the attacker's tx pending cannot be timed (in-block evidence only).","chain":"ethereum","verdict":"confirmed-onchain","t0_ms":1628578498000,"pre_merge":true,"premerge_note":"Pre-Merge: no relays/slots. Flashbots MEV-geth bundles. blocks.flashbots.net answers HTTP 410 (decommissioned); bundle membership below is INFERRED (`inferred_bundle_like`) from coinbase transfers + gas price, not authoritative.","slot":null,"block":{"number":12995895,"hash":"0x8389ac2aff2c08f8ffb173419a7e85c5e1708526834b984b84e104f28e9dc219","ts_ms":1628578498000,"ntx":159,"builder":"ethermine-europe-west3","fee_recipient":"0xea674fdde714fd979de3edf0f56aa9716b898ec8","gas_used":10415169,"base_fee_gwei":30.028855005,"raw":{"block":"raw/rpc/block_12995895.json","receipts":"raw/rpc/receipts_12995895.json","trace":"raw/rpc/trace_block_12995895.json","slot":null}},"strip":[[0,1,"",0.0,0.0],[1,1,"",12.971,0.0],[2,1,"",0.0,0.0087],[3,1,"builder",0.0,0.0],[4,1,"builder",0.0,0.0],[5,1,"builder",0.0,0.0],[6,1,"builder",0.0,0.0],[7,1,"",135.971,0.0],[8,1,"",135.971,0.0],[9,1,"",135.971,0.0],[10,1,"",135.971,0.0],[11,1,"",42.637,0.0],[12,1,"",40.825,0.0],[13,1,"",35.971,0.0],[14,1,"",35.971,0.0],[15,1,"",35.971,0.0],[16,1,"",35.971,0.0],[17,1,"",35.971,0.0],[18,1,"",35.971,0.0],[19,1,"",35.971,0.0],[20,1,"",35.971,0.0],[21,1,"",35.971,0.0],[22,1,"",35.971,0.0],[23,1,"",35.971,0.0],[24,1,"",35.971,0.0],[25,1,"",35.971,0.0],[26,1,"",35.971,0.0],[27,1,"",35.971,0.0],[28,1,"",35.971,0.0],[29,1,"",35.971,0.0],[30,1,"",29.016,0.0],[31,1,"",27.971,0.0],[32,1,"",27.971,0.0],[33,1,"",27.971,0.0],[34,1,"",27.971,0.0],[35,1,"",27.971,0.0],[36,1,"",27.971,0.0],[37,1,"",24.971,0.0],[38,1,"",21.971,0.0],[39,1,"",19.971,0.0],[40,1,"",19.371,0.0],[41,1,"",19.371,0.0],[42,1,"",17.971,0.0],[43,1,"",17.971,0.0],[44,1,"",17.971,0.0],[45,1,"",15.971,0.0],[46,0,"",14.971,0.0],[47,1,"",14.825,0.0],[48,1,"