,058.381173 USDT and 1,954,191.544043 DAI ($4,954,249.93) to Punk's deployer wallet, after Punk messaged the bot EOA at 12:03Z (it first thought the bot was the attacker) and the bot answered 'I frontran the real attacker' at 13:45Z. Before returning, at 19:17:54Z, the bot sold 1,000,000 DAI for 319.1843 ETH on 1inch: the $1M finder's fee Punk agreed ('after paying a fee of 1M DAI up to approximately 16% of the retrieved'). ETH figures here are stablecoin amounts divided by 3,119.7 USD/ETH (the attacker's 1inch rate). Share of the $8.95M drained: 55.4%; of the bot's own USDT+DAI take: 83.2%. The $2.996M USDC the bot mis-sent to the attacker was not recovered (sold for 960.3 ETH, 968 ETH to Tornado Cash); the attacker also took 45,100 DAI in a second tx and ignored Punk's on-chain message.","returned_pct":55.355},"incident_raw":{"block":"raw/rpc/block_12995895.json","receipts":"raw/rpc/receipts_12995895.json","trace_block":"raw/rpc/trace_block_12995895.json","contract_creation":"raw/etherscan/punk_contract_creation.json","model_source":"raw/etherscan/punk_usdc_model_source.json"},"timeline_notes":[],"sources":["https://rekt.news/punkprotocol-rekt","https://halborn.com/explained-the-punk-protocol-hack-august-2021/","https://medium.com/punkprotocol/punk-finance-fair-launch-incident-report-984d9e340eb (HTTP 403 live; read via web.archive.org capture 20211124)","https://etherscan.io/tx/0x7604c7dd6e9bcdba8bac277f1f8e7c1e4c6bb57afd4ddf6a16f629e8495a0281","https://etherscan.io/tx/0x597d11c05563611cb4ad4ed4c57ca53bbe3b7d3fefc37d1ef0724ad58904742b"],"dataset_money":{"scope":"bot-tx","coinbase_eth":0.0,"paid_to_builder_eth":0.01028019784235034,"builder_refund_eth":null,"note":"Scope = the bot tx. gross_loot_eth covers everything it took from the pools ($8,950,039); 2,995,825 USDC of that was sent on to the attacker by the bot's copy error, so the bot's own side is $5,954,214 (bot_net_eth = that / 3,119.7 minus the tx's gas fee 0.03348 ETH, of which 0.01028 ETH tip to the miner